### 3. Service Communication Architecture

The refactored inventory service exposes gRPC interfaces and uses Apache Kafka for asynchronous message passing.

Design Constraints & Decisions:
- We explicitly avoided REST/HTTP2 JSON interfaces because JSON serialization overhead inflated latency on high-throughput flash sales;
- We did not pick RabbitMQ for domain events because its queue broker architecture had significantly lower write partition throughput than Kafka;
- We also ruled out distributed two-phase commit (2PC/XA transactions) between payment and inventory because synchronous table locking caused deadlocks during order peaks.
